{"id":1769490,"retrievedAt":"2026-09-13T15:10:13.178Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/7c1vAM9UU0S7r7DSOz8VlCNrEh8.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1769490,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["JP"],"original_language":"ja","original_title":"BiSH SPARKS “My BiSH Forever” EPiSODE 6 at 大阪城ホール","overview":"BiSH SPARKS “My BiSH Forever” EPiSODE 6 records the arena show the Japanese idol group BiSH played at Osaka-Jo Hall on 21 July 2021 — the second night of a two-day stand and one instalment of BiSH SPARKS, a run of stand-alone arena concerts the group staged across 2021 but pointedly never billed as a tour. It was BiSH's second headline show at the hall and their first there since “And yet BiSH moves.” in September 2019. A catwalk ringed the entire floor, letting Cent Chihiro Chittiii, AiNA THE END, Momoko Gumi Company, Hashiyasume Atsuko, Lingling and Ayuni D circuit the arena. The set opens with “BiSH -Hoshi ga Matataku Yoru ni-” and drives on through “stereo future”, “Promise the Star” and “GiANT KiLLERS”, and “STACKiNG”, the theme to the anime Kingdom, gets its live premiere. A time-loop comedy skit in which Hashiyasume Atsuko turns into a takoyaki splits the set, and twenty-one songs end on “ALL YOU NEED IS LOVE”.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/3P0oxrIDf23tpTn5M1fE4jtCi9n.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"","revenue":0,"runtime":0,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"BiSH SPARKS My BiSH Forever EPiSODE 6 at Osaka-Jo Hall","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"external_ids":{"imdb_id":null,"wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"keywords":{"keywords":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":1,"id":2284032,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Cent Chihiro Chittiii","original_name":"セントチヒロ・チッチ","popularity":0.4484,"profile_path":"/6ElXLkaBILn8c